Z||000000||jlhuber||10-20-1999||10:07 PM||||ok all you fiero guru's(spelling?).  couple of questions for you.  will the stock 3spd automatic transaxle from an '86.5 gt hold up to 270-300hp emitting from the 60 degree v6?  if not , what will?  if yes, where can i get the best shift kit to make her snap hard when she shifts?  all in all, i've got a lot of ponies, but don't know if i can sucsessfuly put it to the gruond with the 'ole 3spd trnsxl.  oh yeah, incase you haven't noticed, i can't spell worth beens.||||reg||6
Z||000001||batboy||10-20-1999||11:30 PM||||The auto tranny is fairly tough, but will break down if abused a lot with a powerful engine, same as any of the other trannies available for the Fiero. I have an auto in my V8 Fiero. The previous owner blew out the original tranny, but he admitted to driving the piss out of it. To be on the safe side, I don't do burnouts or holeshots. I'm looking for a good shift kit too. Any recommendations guys?||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||10-21-1999||09:37 AM||||<A HREF="http://www.teleport.com./~txchange/index.shtml" TARGET=_blank>TRANSMISSION EXCHANGE CO</A> has TransoGo kits. These are one of the few I know of. I know nothing about the kit but that they usually have them in stock.<P>No GM FWD auto tranny that fits in these cars is going to take abuse. Especially a bone stock one. Even with a shift kit it's still a stock tranny. It will just shift differantly. You should have the tranny rebuilt with racing in mind. Even then there is only so much you can do to it.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Eric Marsh||10-21-1999||01:23 PM||||Check out Jim's Performance Transmissions. (517) 663-0578. He is doing the heavy duty rebuilds for Archie's V8 kits. I've got one of his trans myself, though its too early to know how well it will work out.||||reg||6
